---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
import CounterIllustration from "../../components/CounterIllustration.astro";
import GCounterDemo from "../../components/GCounterDemo.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import {
  eventualConsistencyTerm,
  gCounterTerm,
  replicaTerm,
} from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="G-counter"
  description="Alice, Bob, and Carol count birds on separate trails. A G-counter preserves their independent sightings despite late, repeated, or reordered notes."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="G-counter"
>
  <article class="structure-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structures</p>
      <h1>G-counter</h1>
      <p class="structure-summary">
        The ranger asks Alice, Bob, and Carol to count birds on three trails.
        Each hiker tracks their own sightings in a shared three-row format,
        then leaves notes with their name and running count. The notes may
        arrive late, out of order, or more than once. By the end of the hike,
        all three notebooks must show the same total.
      </p>
      <LessonIllustration id="structures-g-counter" />
    </header>

    <nav class="lesson-map" aria-label="G-counter lesson map">
      <a href="#notebook-setup-title">Understand the notebooks</a>
      <a href="#race-title">See crossing notes</a>
      <a href="#gcounter-demo-title">Try the sandbox</a>
    </nav>

    <section aria-labelledby="notebook-setup-title">
      <h2 id="notebook-setup-title">Three hikers copy the same notebook</h2>
      <p>
        Each notebook has one row for Alice, one for Bob, and one for Carol.
        A hiker writes new sightings in their own row. The other rows record
        the latest running counts received from checkpoint notes.
      </p>
      <figure class="notebook notebook-setup">
        <table aria-label="The hikers' notebooks before they share notes">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Row</th>
              <th scope="col">Alice's notebook</th>
              <th scope="col">Bob's notebook</th>
              <th scope="col">Carol's notebook</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Alice</th><td>7</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Bob</th><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>0</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Carol</th><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr>
            <tr class="notebook-total">
              <th scope="row">Birds seen</th><td>7</td><td>3</td><td>0</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <figcaption>
          Before the first notes arrive, each hiker knows only their own
          running count.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        Alice does not send seven separate sightings. She leaves one
        cumulative note that says her row has reached 7. Bob leaves the same
        kind of note when his row reaches 3.
      </p>
      <div
        class="checkpoint-notes"
        role="group"
        aria-label="Checkpoint note examples"
      >
        <p><strong>Alice</strong><span>Running bird count</span><output>7</output></p>
        <p><strong>Bob</strong><span>Running bird count</span><output>3</output></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <StructureFacts
      family="CRDT"
      model="State-based convergent replicated data type"
      updates="Increment only"
      merge="Keep the largest count from each replica, then sum the components."
      delivery="Safe under repeated and out-of-order delivery"
      bestFor="Distributed tallies that never decrease"
      cost="One integer for each replica"
    />
    <CounterIllustration kind="g-counter" />

    <section aria-labelledby="one-counter-title">
      <h2 id="one-counter-title">Alice fills in her row</h2>
      <p>
        Alice takes the ridge trail. Each time she spots a bird, she adds one
        to her row. After seven sightings, Alice's notebook reads
        <code>[Alice: 7, Bob: 0, Carol: 0]</code>, so her local total is 7.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alice's local copy of the shared counter is a{" "}
        <dfn><a href="/glossary/#replica">replica</a></dfn>. Bob and Carol each
        keep their own replica. The hikers exchange cumulative messages by
        leaving notes at known checkpoints.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...replicaTerm} />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="second-counter-title">
      <h2 id="second-counter-title">Bob takes a different trail</h2>
      <p>
        Bob counts birds along the river trail. Alice changes only Alice's
        count, and Bob changes only Bob's count. If Alice has seen 7 birds and
        Bob has seen 3, their shared total is 10.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a grow-only counter, or{" "}
        <dfn><a href="/glossary/#g-counter">G-counter</a></dfn>. Each replica
        keeps the largest note it has received from each hiker, then adds those
        counts. It does not add every message. If Bob leaves the same
        checkpoint note twice, both messages contain the same count of 3
        birds. His count stays 3.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...gCounterTerm} />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="race-title">
      <h2 id="race-title">Their checkpoint notes cross</h2>
      <p>
        When a hiker finds a note, they copy its running count into the named
        row only if the number is larger than the count already there. The
        three rows add up to the bird count.
      </p>
      <p>
        On Carol's route, the first note at the north fork is from
        Alice: 7 birds. At the river bridge, she finds Bob's note for 3. Carol
        has not seen a bird herself, so her own row stays at 0.
      </p>
      <figure class="notebook">
        <table aria-label="Carol's notebook at each checkpoint">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Checkpoint and note</th>
              <th scope="col">Alice</th>
              <th scope="col">Bob</th>
              <th scope="col">Carol</th>
              <th scope="col">Total</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Trailhead</th><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">North fork: Alice 7</th><td>7</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>7</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">River bridge: Bob 3</th><td>7</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>10</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Old lookout: Alice 4</th><td>7</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>10</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <figcaption>
          Carol updates her notebook as she reaches each checkpoint.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        At the old lookout, Carol finds an earlier note from Alice with a count of 4.
        Her notebook already contains 7, so she leaves that row alone:
        <code>max(7, 4) = 7</code>. Had she found 4 first, the row would have
        changed from 0 to 4, then from 4 to 7. Either path through the notes
        leads to the same notebook and the same total.
      </p>
      <p>
        Elsewhere on the trails, the three notebooks can still disagree. Alice
        may know only her 7, Bob only his 3, and Carol neither. In the sandbox,
        record sightings for any hiker and control when notes arrive. The
        worked example leaves Alice's and Bob's notes together.
      </p>
    </section>

    <GCounterDemo />

    <section aria-labelledby="result-title">
      <h2 id="result-title">Every trail catches up</h2>
      <p>
        After delivery of both checkpoint notes, Alice, Bob, and Carol all read
        10. Their views were temporarily inconsistent, but the G-counter kept
        both hikers' observations and made every replica agree.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is{" "}
        <dfn><a href="/glossary/#eventual-consistency">eventual consistency</a></dfn>.
        For each hiker, merge keeps the larger count from their checkpoint
        notes. The rule is commutative, associative, and idempotent. Arrival
        order does not change the answer, and the network can deliver the same
        checkpoint note more than once.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...eventualConsistencyTerm} />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="limit-title">
      <h2 id="limit-title">The count cannot go down</h2>
      <p>
        Every hiker needs a unique replica ID. If two hikers share an ID,
        pairwise maximum can discard one concurrent update.
      </p>
      <p>
        The merge rule can only keep or raise each component. If a hiker finds
        a counting mistake, lowering a component is unsafe because an older,
        larger note could restore the mistake. The next structure records
        corrections without changing this merge rule.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="notes-title">
      <h2 id="notes-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        This lesson calls Watershed's public{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/g_counter_kernel.gleam">G-counter kernel</a>.
        The G-counter merge rule keeps the largest cumulative count for each
        hiker.
      </p>
      <p>
        The merge rule is the state-based grow-only counter described in{" "}
        <a href="https://inria.hal.science/inria-00555588/document">A comprehensive study of Convergent and Commutative Replicated Data Types</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through structures">
      <a href="/structures/counters/">Back to counter family</a>
      <a href="/structures/pn-counter/">Continue to PN-counter</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .structure-page {
    max-width: var(--measure-reading);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .structure-page > section {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }

  .lesson-map {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-block: var(--space-5) var(--space-7);
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .lesson-map a {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: var(--space-3);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .lesson-map a + a {
    border-inline-start: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  .structure-summary {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  pre {
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--clear) 45%, var(--sky-sheet));
  }

  .notebook {
    margin-block: var(--space-5);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .notebook table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 36rem;
    border-collapse: collapse;
  }

  .notebook :is(th, td) {
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line-faint);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .notebook td {
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .notebook tbody tr:last-child :is(th, td) {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .notebook-setup .notebook-total :is(th, td) {
    border-top: calc(var(--rule-width) * 2) solid var(--line);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .notebook figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .checkpoint-notes {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .checkpoint-notes p {
    display: grid;
    min-width: 12rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--clear) 45%, var(--sky-sheet));
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
  }

  .checkpoint-notes strong {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .checkpoint-notes span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .checkpoint-notes output {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .structure-next {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .structure-next a {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (width < 40rem) {
    .lesson-map {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .lesson-map a + a {
      border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
      border-inline-start: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
